{"id":"capability-09256362696334557463","name":"Using Policy Plus","purpose":"Start the program, restore its saved settings and leave it again.","membershipRule":"Entry points that start or close the program as a whole and restore its own settings (startup, exit). Dialog-specific behaviour belongs to the capability of that dialog's business area; loading definitions belongs to managing policy definitions.","evidence":[{"file":"PolicyPlus/Main.vb","firstLine":18,"lastLine":45}]}
{"id":"capability-94819467697830882144","name":"Managing policy definitions","purpose":"Load, download and inspect the policy definition files (ADMX/ADML) and the products and support rules they declare.","membershipRule":"Entry points that load policy definitions from a folder, download the Microsoft ADMX package, choose the ADML language, or list and show details of loaded definition files, categories, products, support definitions and policy elements. Searching and filtering the policy list belongs to finding and browsing policies; changing policy values belongs to setting policies.","evidence":[{"file":"PolicyPlus/DownloadAdmx.vb","firstLine":33,"lastLine":130},{"file":"PolicyPlus/Main.vb","firstLine":510,"lastLine":523}]}
{"id":"capability-95522755523734389125","name":"Finding and browsing policies","purpose":"Browse policies by category and find them by text, ID, registry location or filter.","membershipRule":"Entry points that navigate the category tree and policy list, search policies (by ID, text, registry key/value) and show results, or configure the filter that narrows the list. Does not change policy values or definition files.","evidence":[{"file":"PolicyPlus/FindByText.vb","firstLine":11,"lastLine":73}]}
{"id":"capability-52723301806026979742","name":"Setting policies","purpose":"Choose a policy's state and option values and apply them to a computer, user or policy file, including SPOL text import and inspection.","membershipRule":"Entry points of the policy setting editor (state, options, list editor, section switch, apply) and of importing or showing a policy's settings as SPOL text. Raw registry-value editing of a policy file and REG import/export belong to editing policy files directly.","evidence":[{"file":"PolicyPlus/EditSetting.vb","firstLine":312,"lastLine":315},{"file":"PolicyPlus/ImportSpol.vb","firstLine":3,"lastLine":10}]}
{"id":"capability-96720013561244733699","name":"Editing policy files directly","purpose":"Edit the raw keys and values of a policy (POL) file and import or export them as REG scripts.","membershipRule":"Entry points of the raw POL editor and its key, value and delete dialogs, and the REG import and export dialogs. Choosing a policy's setting through its definition belongs to setting policies.","evidence":[{"file":"PolicyPlus/EditPol.vb","firstLine":113,"lastLine":129},{"file":"PolicyPlus/EditPol.vb","firstLine":276,"lastLine":278}]}
